NOTE: This Version of Kawa is Modified for App Inventor
-------------------------------------------------------

To compile and build Kawa for App Inventor run "ant appinventor".

Build with a Java 8 JDK and target Java 7, as App Inventor's jar has always been:

    ant -Dant.build.javac.source=1.7 -Dant.build.javac.target=1.7 appinventor

Newer JDKs fail: on Java 14+ java.lang.Record clashes with Kawa's Record, and on
Java 9+ kawa/lib/kawa/regex.scm hits an ambiguous Matcher.replaceAll overload.
Compiling Kawa's Scheme libraries against newer JDK classes could also link them
to methods that older Android versions lack.

This builds two jars:

  kawa-1.11-compiler.jar The full jar. App Inventor's buildserver compiles YAIL
                         with it (kawa.repl -C).
  kawa-1.11-runtime.jar  The classes an app can load on the device, for dexing.
                         It leaves out the classes listed in
                         classes-to-skip-for-appinventor-runtime: other languages,
                         the servlet and SAX glue, and SRFI libraries that only
                         (require 'srfi-N) loads, which YAIL never emits.

When Kawa's sources change, regenerate the list from the compiler jar:

    python3 appinventor-runtime-classes.py kawa-1.11-compiler.jar > classes-to-skip-for-appinventor-runtime

KAWA, THE JAVA-BASED SCHEME SYSTEM
----------------------------------

Kawa is an implementation of the Scheme programming language.
It is implemented in Java, and compiles Scheme into Java byte-codes.

The Kawa home page is: http://www.gnu.org/software/kawa/
This explains how to build, install, and use Kawa.
A copy of the documentation is in the doc directory.

See http://www.gnu.org/software/kawa/news.html for recent changes.

Kawa's copyright is in the file COPYING.

	--Per Bothner
